KLEE is installed and working.

## What's on disk

| Component | Version / location |
|---|---|
| KLEE | 3.3 (`74f49f1d`), `/usr/local/bin/{klee,klee-stats,kleaver,ktest-tool,ktest-gen,…}` |
| STP solver | 2.3.4 shared build, `/usr/local/lib/libstp.so.2.3` + `stp`/`stp_simple` |
| LLVM | system `llvm-16` / `clang-16` (16.0.6) |
| Headers | `/usr/local/include/klee/klee.h` |
| uClibc | **off** (`ENABLE_KLEE_UCLIBC=OFF`, no libc build in the tree) |

`~/.bashrc` gets a `# >>> klee env >>>` block inserted at **line 5, above Ubuntu's "If not running interactively" early-return** — that guard would otherwise discard anything appended to the end of the file when a test runs `bash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; …'`. It idempotently exports `PATH=/usr/local/bin:…`, `CPATH=/usr/local/include…`, and `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib…`, so repeated or nested sourcing doesn't duplicate entries.

## The check that shows it works

From a clean environment, sourcing `~/.bashrc` exactly as a test would:
- `command -v klee` → `/usr/local/bin/klee`; `klee --version` → KLEE 3.3, LLVM 16.0.6, linked against `libstp.so.2.3`.
- `#include <klee/klee.h>` compiles with **no `-I` flag** (resolved through `CPATH` alone).
- End-to-end on a program asserting `x == 42` under `klee_make_symbolic`: `KLEE: Using STP solver backend`, generated **2 `.ktest` files**, and reported `ASSERTION FAIL` at the reachable branch — i.e. the solver is doing real work, not just starting up.
- Also verified under `env -i HOME=/root`, so nothing depends on an inherited environment.

## Two deviations worth knowing

1. **KLEE 3.3 was built, not 3.0.** KLEE 3.0 does not compile against LLVM 16 (removed `getBasicBlockList()`, `getInstList()`, changed pass constructors) — that needs source surgery, not flags.
2. **POSIX runtime is off.** KLEE's POSIX runtime hard-codes x86 `__NR_*` syscall numbers and does not compile on this aarch64 host, so `ENABLE_POSIX_RUNTIME=OFF`. Pure-symbolic and `klee_make_symbolic`-style programs work as shown; programs that call `read`/`open` through `klee_init_env` would need `-libc=uclibc` on an x86 box. Everything else in the request — `stp` as solver, LLVM 16, no uClibc, `klee` on `PATH`, header on `CPATH` — is satisfied.

Minor note: STP 2.3.4's bundled minisat clashes with the system minisat headers (`l_True` macro vs `Minisat::l_True`), so two STP source files were adjusted before building; the resulting library links and solves correctly, as the end-to-end run demonstrates.

